{"agent":"fleet-stuck","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`drop_command` rebuilds the dependent's **entire** needs list from its current needs minus the single gone id (`rest = \",\".join(n for n in item.needs if n != dep_id)`), and `--needs` is by construction a replacement of that list. When one open item needs two already-gone dependencies, the commands produced for that item are mutually contradictory, and doctor prints all of them as the fix:\n\n- Input: `X.needs == [A, B]`, both A and B abandoned (or removed), X open.\n- `stuck_edges(st)` yields `(\"X\", \"A\", 'ddflow update X --needs \"B\"')` and `(\"X\", \"B\", 'ddflow update X --needs \"A\"')`.\n- `health.py` appends both lines, each phrased as \"so X is stuck for good: `…`\"; the same pair is emitted in the `drop_edges` list of the abandon/remove event payloads.\n\nApplying the first command leaves X needing B (still gone), and applying the second then re-adds A, which the first command had just dropped. After following every command doctor printed, X still has a needs edge to a gone item and the finding is reported again — the advertised remedy does not clear it. This is not a corner case for this bug: the report itself counts only 9 of 67 tasks as blocked by \"nothing else\", i.e. the majority have additional blocked reasons, and an item needing two abandoned `decide` tasks produces exactly this input. The remedy needs to drop all gone edges for the item in one command (e.g. `--needs` with only the still-live needs), or the commands must be produced/applied cumulatively rather than each re-deriving from the stale full needs list.","digest":"89ff620fe5e05eb3","location":"ddflow/core/stuck.py:16 (`drop_command`), used by ddflow/api/reporting/health.py:92 and the abandon/remove payloads","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/core/stuck.py:16 (`drop_command`), used by ddflow/api/reporting/health.py:92 and the abandon/remove payloads"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"`_stranded_line` returns the empty string whenever `out.data[\"drop_edges\"]` is empty/absent, even if `out.data[\"stranded\"]` names dependents that are stuck for good. For a task whose *only* `needs` entry is the item being abandoned/removed, there is no remaining prerequisite to re-point to, so the generated fix command is either omitted or degenerates to an empty `--needs \"\"` (which the command builder is unlikely to emit), leaving `drop_edges` empty. In that case `ddflow abandon D1` / `ddflow remove D1` prints only `\"D1 abandoned: <reason>\"` and drops the `warning: ... still need(s) D1 and can never start` line entirely — i.e. the code falls back to precisely the silent behaviour the bug (B9eeecd134c) is about, for the \"nothing else\" dependents (9 of 67 on 2026-10-15) that doctor now has to report alone. The new test `tests/test_abandoned_prereq.py::test_abandon_warns_naming_dependents_and_still_succeeds` cannot detect this because `_seed()` always gives the dependent a second open prerequisite (`needs=\"D1,D2\"`), and the sole test with `needs=\"\"` has no stranded dependents at all; no case covers \"stranded non-empty, no re-point target\". The gate should key off `out.data[\"stranded\"]` (which is present in both the abandon and remove payloads added by this diff) and only conditionally append the commands.","digest":"79838b7a118d986b","location":"ddflow/surfaces/declared/lifecycle_cli.py:_stranded_line","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/declared/lifecycle_cli.py:_stranded_line"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":8889,"diff_sha":"4c6eba9ce45ea59ca6f5810905978792f650c725508f4d6844960e593a5ff48c","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":303.6,"family":"deepseek","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"2eb9885e7f5d8bb7","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B9eeecd134c.critic.lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash.20261015T130116Z-a63a39b5.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"517cdb0d660e5191f29870a3f572131f7bc0c7ab","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/core/stuck.py:16 (`drop_command`), used by ddflow/api/reporting/health.py:92 and the abandon/remove payloads","ddflow/surfaces/declared/lifecycle_cli.py:_stranded_line"],"tree_sha":"16e5c6ca0dd0+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e3e41ecf6f153c47dc4516bf3","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":63168,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B9eeecd134c","ts":"2026-10-15T13:06:20.832315Z"}
